# Half time - the leaving track pulled down to half speed, then cut on the bar.
#
# Not the brake, which stops dead and is a tape stop. This lands on a ratio the music
# actually has - half - so the last two bars are the same record an octave down and at
# half the tempo, which still keeps time with the room while very obviously ending.
#
# `speed` drags the pitch with it by design (see the control's own note): the pitch
# falling *is* the effect, and correcting it would leave a track playing slowly for no
# audible reason.

name    Half time
note    the leaving track dropped an octave, then cut
bars    4
align   beat
tempo   match
power   free

lane out gain
    bar 0    1.0    hold
    bar 3    1.0    hold
    bar 4    0.0    hold

lane out speed
    bar 0    1.0    hold
    bar 2    1.0    smooth
    bar 3    0.5    hold
    bar 4    0.5    hold

# Its top end goes with its speed, because a half-speed record is a dull one and leaving
# the hats up would give the trick away before it lands.
lane out lowpass
    bar 0   16000   smooth
    bar 3    4000   hold
    bar 4    4000   hold

# The new track is already there underneath, at its own speed, so the cut is a cut to
# something rather than to nothing.
lane in gain
    bar 0    0.0    power-up
    bar 3    1.0    hold
    bar 4    1.0    hold

lane in tempo
    bar 0    0.0    hold
    bar 3    0.0    smooth
    bar 4    1.0    hold

hook bar 2    toast ½ half time
